    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0253" n="139" xml:id="pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Latvia/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-20T12:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 1:24 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>183. Minister of Finance has informed me that the Cabinet of Ministers has
                    decided to inaugurate funding negotiations through the Latvian consul at New
                        York.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d79-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d79-f1" n="6" xml:id="d79-f1-content">
                <p>Minister Coleman informed the Department by despatch of Jan. 28, 1925, that Mr.
                    Ringold Kalning, formerly Latvian Minister of Finance, would proceed to the
                    United States as Commissioner to assist the consul in the funding negotiations
                    (file no. 800.51 W 89 Latvia/36).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
